Backport of the upstream main fix for a C ABI mismatch present in
ghostty v1.2.3–v1.3.1: include/ghostty.h declares
`void ghostty_surface_free_text(ghostty_surface_t, ghostty_text_s*)`
(two parameters) but the Zig export only accepted the text pointer.
C callers therefore passed the *surface* pointer where the impl
expected the Text struct, so `Text.deinit` inspected surface memory
(text field offset happens to read as null — silent no-op) and the
buffer allocated by `dumpTextLocked` was never freed. Every
`ghostty_surface_read_text` / `ghostty_surface_read_selection` call
leaked its full dumped text. Pier polls viewport text (agent state
probes) at 250ms per active agent terminal, which compounds this into
gigabytes of main-process memory over long sessions.

diff --git a/src/apprt/embedded.zig b/src/apprt/embedded.zig
--- a/src/apprt/embedded.zig
+++ b/src/apprt/embedded.zig
@@ -1761,7 +1761,7 @@
         return true;
     }
 
-    export fn ghostty_surface_free_text(ptr: *Text) void {
+    export fn ghostty_surface_free_text(_: *Surface, ptr: *Text) void {
         ptr.deinit();
     }
 
